facts:
Adding $c$ shifts the whole curve **up** ($c>0$) or **down** ($c<0$), carrying its asymptote with it.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-5, xmax=4.8, ymin=-1.5, ymax=8.4, samples=120, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[thick, dashed, <->, domain=-5:1.8] {exp(x*ln(2))};
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-5:2.2] {exp(x*ln(2))+2};
\addplot[dashed, red, domain=-5:4.8] {2};
\node[anchor=west] at (axis cs:2.1,3.48) {$y=a^{x}$};
\node[anchor=east, blue] at (axis cs:4.7,7.9) {$y=a^{x}+c$};
\node[anchor=north east, red] at (axis cs:4.7,1.85) {$y=c$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$y=-a^{x}$ is $y=a^{x}$ **reflected in the $x$-axis**, and its asymptote stays $y=0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4.6, xmax=4.8, ymin=-5.5, ymax=5.5, samples=120, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[thick, dashed, <->, domain=-4.6:2.1] {exp(x*ln(2))};
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-3.6:2.1] {-exp(x*ln(2))};
\node[anchor=west] at (axis cs:2.3,4.29) {$y=a^{x}$};
\node[anchor=west, blue] at (axis cs:2.3,-4.29) {$y=-a^{x}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$y=a^{-x}$ is $y=a^{x}$ **reflected in the $y$-axis**, turning growth into **decay** when $a>1$, and its asymptote stays $y=0$. When $0<a<1$, replacing $x$ with $-x$ turns decay into growth.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4.8, xmax=4.8, ymin=-1.5, ymax=5.5, samples=120, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[thick, dashed, <->, domain=-4.0:2.1] {exp(x*ln(2))};
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-2.1:4.0] {exp(x*ln(0.5))};
\node[anchor=west] at (axis cs:2.3,4.29) {$y=a^{x}$};
\node[anchor=east, blue] at (axis cs:-2.3,4.29) {$y=a^{-x}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

